# Secrets of this OverLyX instance — copy to deploy/secrets.env (git-ignored, chmod 600). The
# systemd unit reads it via EnvironmentFile=; the nightly backup keeps a copy. The file lives on the
# server only: to set up another machine, scp it, or re-create the values (see README ▸ Secrets).
# systemd syntax: KEY=value, no quotes needed, no `export`.

# "Sign in with Google" (OAuth redirect URI: <OVERLYX_PUBLIC_URL>/api/auth/google/callback)
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Help ▸ Report a problem and automatic error reports become GitHub issues of GITHUB_REPO.
# A fine-grained personal access token with "Issues: read and write" on that repository is enough.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
#GITHUB_REPO=japhba/overlyx

# Literature search in the citation dialog. Without keys: OpenAlex + DBLP (mediocre relevance).
# Semantic Scholar (free key, Scholar-like relevance): https://www.semanticscholar.org/product/api#api-key-form
S2_API_KEY=
# Real Google Scholar results through SerpApi (https://serpapi.com; free tier 100 searches/month)
SERPAPI_KEY=

# "Escalate to AI" document repair (Review ▸ Escalate to AI…): calls OpenRouter (https://openrouter.ai/keys)
# with the broken .tex file + the OverLyX format spec, and proposes a fix for you to review before applying.
# Without a key, the feature is hidden (POST /docs/*/ai-repair returns 503).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
#OPENROUTER_REPAIR_MODEL=anthropic/claude-opus-5
# The same key also powers the editor's AI assistance (⌘K rewrite, autocomplete — opt-in per browser
# under Tools ▸ AI). Gemini 3.7 Flash rewrites; autocomplete uses 2.5 Flash Lite (0.5–1 s vs 2.6 s, and it actually proposes sentences).
#OVERLYX_AI_MODEL=google/gemini-3.7-flash
#OVERLYX_AI_COMPLETION_MODEL=google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite
